      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/0002/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>0002</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/0002/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="About the manual">About the manual</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors />
                <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/0004/</fr:uri>
                <fr:display-uri>0004</fr:display-uri>
                <fr:route>/0004/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="Principles">Principles</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>The geolog manual is an <html:em>authoratative</html:em>, <html:em>conceptual</html:em>, and <html:em>incomplete</html:em> reference document for engaged users and developers of geolog.</html:p>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/0005/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>0005</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/0005/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="Authoratative">Authoratative</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Principle</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>When the manual makes a definitive statement about the behavior of geolog, if the code deviates from the manual then the code is considered to have a bug.</html:p>
                    <html:p>There may be points in the manual where as I am writing, I decide that the current behavior of geolog is inadequate. In these places, I will write down what I intend the behavior to be, and mark the sentence with <html:sup class="smallcaps">todo</html:sup> at the end.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/0006/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>0006</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/0006/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="Conceptual">Conceptual</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Principle</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>The purpose of the manual is to produce <html:em>understanding</html:em>. The manual is not a specification, but a motivated reader could probably fill in the full details of a specification from the understanding imparted in the manual. Most importantly, a user of geolog who has carefully read the manual should not need to guess at what any particular piece of code means; the conceptual understanding laid out in this manual should be sufficient to give an unambiguous human-comprehensible semantics.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/0007/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>0007</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/0007/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="Incomplete">Incomplete</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Principle</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>This manual (like geolog itself) is currently incomplete.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <html:p>The geolog manual is <html:em>not</html:em> a tutorial. The geolog manual is <html:em>not</html:em> a place for original mathematical research. The geolog manual is <html:em>not</html:em> a development log.</html:p>
                <html:p>Moreover, the geolog manual is <html:em>not</html:em> an advertisement. The intended audience of this manual is a reader with patience and a good amount of time, who is motivated for reasons found elsewhere to learn about geolog. There may be sections where we outline the <html:em>rationale</html:em> for a design decision; these should not be interpreted as claims of the superiority of this design decision, merely as a record of the thought process that went into it.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors />
                <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/0008/</fr:uri>
                <fr:display-uri>0008</fr:display-uri>
                <fr:route>/0008/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="Meta">Meta</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>The geolog manual is written in <fr:link href="/forester/" title="Forester" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/forester/" display-uri="forester" type="local">Forester</fr:link>. Forester is a very flexible tool that can be used in many ways. In order for the manual to achieve its goals, it is necessary to put constraints on the use of forester.</html:p>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/0009/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>0009</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/0009/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="Address usage">Address usage</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Constraint</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>We use a single address namespace without prefixes, similar to <fr:link href="/stacks-project/" title="The Stacks Project" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/stacks-project/" display-uri="stacks-project" type="local">The Stacks Project</fr:link>. This means that creating new pages requires obtaining a “global lock” on the “next address” counter. Currently, Owen is holding this global lock; when more people are working on the manual we will coordinate around address allocation.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/000A/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>000A</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/000A/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="Global linear ordering">Global linear ordering</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Constraint</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>The entire manual is meant to be kept in a single global hierarchy rooted at the <fr:link href="/0001/" title="Geolog manual" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/0001/" display-uri="0001" type="local">home page</fr:link>.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/000F/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>000F</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/000F/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="Glossary and index">Glossary and index</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Constraint</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>The manual contains a combination <fr:link href="/0003/" title="Glossary and index" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/0003/" display-uri="0003" type="local">glossary and index</fr:link>, which collects technical terms used throughout the manual.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/000J/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>000J</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/000J/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="Lack of tree metadata">Lack of tree metadata</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Constraint</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>This manual is meant to be a single document with a single voice. Therefore, we do not put author metadata on individual trees, and all trees are considered to have been written by the geolog project. Moreover, we omit dates on non-reference trees; the manual as a whole should be considered as current, and out-of-date trees should be edited or deleted.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <html:p>More generally, the geolog manual should be thought of as more of a <fr:link href="/hyperbook/" title="Hyperbook" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/hyperbook/" display-uri="hyperbook" type="local">Hyperbook</fr:link> than a <fr:link href="/zettelkasten/" title="Zettelkasten" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/zettelkasten/" display-uri="zettelkasten" type="local">Zettelkasten</fr:link>.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors />
                <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/000B/</fr:uri>
                <fr:display-uri>000B</fr:display-uri>
                <fr:route>/000B/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="Audience">Audience</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>There are a variety of intended audiences for this manual; a given reader may fall into several of the following categories.</html:p>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/000C/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>000C</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/000C/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="The categorical logician">The categorical logician</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Audience</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>The <html:strong>categorical logician</html:strong> is a reader who is comfortable with modern approaches to the categorical semantics of type theory, such as:</html:p>
                    <html:ul><html:li><fr:link href="/shulman-2016-categorical/" title="Categorical logic from a categorical point of view" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/shulman-2016-categorical/" display-uri="shulman-2016-categorical" type="local">Categorical logic from a categorical point of view</fr:link></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:link href="/kovacs-2022-typetheoretic/" title="Type-Theoretic Signatures for Algebraic
Theories and Inductive Types" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/kovacs-2022-typetheoretic/" display-uri="kovacs-2022-typetheoretic" type="local">Type-Theoretic Signatures for Algebraic
Theories and Inductive Types</fr:link></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:link href="/uemura-2021-abstract/" title="Abstract and Concrete Type Theories" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/uemura-2021-abstract/" display-uri="uemura-2021-abstract" type="local">Abstract and Concrete Type Theories</fr:link></html:li></html:ul>
                    <html:p>The categorical logician also has a reasonable grasp of topos theory and 2-category theory.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/000D/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>000D</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/000D/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="The type theorist">The type theorist</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Audience</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>The <html:strong>type theorist</html:strong> is a reader who is comfortable with traditional type theory rules given in Gentzen’s tree notation and who might also have some experience with normalization by evaluation, but who is not yet familiar with the modern approaches of <fr:link href="/000C/" title="The categorical logician" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/000C/" display-uri="000C" type="local">The categorical logician</fr:link>.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/000E/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>000E</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/000E/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="The database engineer">The database engineer</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Audience</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>The <html:strong>database engineer</html:strong> is a reader who does not necessarily know any type theory, but is familiar with <fr:link href="/sql/" title="SQL" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/sql/" display-uri="sql" type="local">SQL</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/datalog/" title="Datalog" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/datalog/" display-uri="datalog" type="local">Datalog</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/conjunctive-queries/" title="Conjunctive queries" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/conjunctive-queries/" display-uri="conjunctive-queries" type="local">Conjunctive queries</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/egglog/" title="Egglog" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/egglog/" display-uri="egglog" type="local">Egglog</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/automerge/" title="Automerge" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/automerge/" display-uri="automerge" type="local">Automerge</fr:link>, and perhaps some of the methods for incrementalizing queries like <fr:link href="/dbsp/" title="DBSP" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/dbsp/" display-uri="dbsp" type="local">DBSP</fr:link>.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/000H/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>000H</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/000H/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="The developer">The developer</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Audience</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>The <html:strong>developer</html:strong> is someone who is interested in contributing to geolog, or creating a geolog-like system.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors />
                    <fr:uri>https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/000G/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>000G</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/000G/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="The programmer-user">The programmer-user</fr:title>
                    <fr:taxon>Audience</fr:taxon>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>The <html:strong>programmer-user</html:strong> is a reader who intends to incorporate geolog into a larger application. The programmer-user should be familiar with the language that they intend to use geolog from (currently, this is only TypeScript), and should be willing to learn a new language. We say “programmer-user” to distinguish this audience from the user of an application that the “programmer-user” creates; this user needs not read this manual.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
                <html:p>The <fr:link href="/000G/" title="The programmer-user" uri="https://manual.geolog.sgai.uk/000G/" display-uri="000G" type="local">programmer-user</fr:link> who also falls into the earlier categories will benefit from a deeper understanding of geolog. However, geolog is also comprehensible in a self-contained way, just as one does not need to understand cartesian closed categories in order to use <html:code>lambda x: x + 1</html:code> in Python, and it is a goal of this manual to present a clear conceptual picture for the non-mathematical programmer-user.</html:p>
                <html:p>At various points in the manual we clarify which audience a certain section is for; a reader not in that audience may safely skip that section.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
